# Off-Season Mini-Cut Protocol

> [!abstract] Owns the short off-season reset.
> This is not the same deployment as a long contest-style cut. It is a small interruption inside a growth phase, mostly using diet structure, step count, glucose tools, and training-load control so the next bulk block starts cleaner.

> [!danger] Boundary
> Harm-reduction documentation, not a prescription. Prescription glucose drugs, SGLT2 inhibitors, thyroid drugs, stimulants, and peptides require the safety gates in their owner protocols before deployment.

## Deployment Clock

| Field | Rule |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Bulk is drifting: waist/BF rising faster than strength, appetite is messy, digestion worsens, glucose tolerance degrades, or weight gain is above target. |
| Duration logic | Short reset. The goal is to restore sensitivity, not live in a deficit. |
| Deployment logic | Tier 1 first: food, steps, glucose control, pump retention, and fatigue management. Avoid spending harsh tools while still high-BF. |
| Stock math | Small pulse demand repeated across long off-seasons. Count it separately from long-cut campaign stock. |

